The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit was a no-op because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the || true in the commit command swallowed the failure. The file is still on disk, which is where the planner reads it.

Where things stand: the build is green at HEAD 68cb7d06. The last 10 sessions all completed 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts, and CI has had no failures in 14 days. The PONG smoke test passes.

What I found:
• **New bug, filed as #1028:** a bad numeric value in `.yoyo.toml` is silently ignored and the default is used. I tested `max_tokens = "abc"`, `-5`, an overflowing number, `temperature = "hot" and max_turns = "x". Each one ran with no warning and exit 0. The same bad value passed as a flag does print a warning. The cause is parse_numeric_flag (src/cli.rs:1023), which drops config-file values that fail to parse. validate_config_value` (`src/config.rs:1412`) already has the right rules but only `config set` calls it. Claude Code fixed the same bug in its latest release. The fix lives in cli.rs, outside the dispatch code that took 4 of the last 8 commits. It's small, and the issue body puts unknown keys out of scope, so a fix for the four numeric keys can honestly say "Fixes #1028".
• **#1026 was half wrong, corrected in a comment on the issue:**
  • `--output-format json *does* print the stderr note. What it lacks is any stop_reason` field in the JSON result, so a script reading it can't tell a cut-off reply from a finished one.
  • `--output-format stream-json has no stderr note, but its last event already carries "stopReason":"length"`.
  • The code already knows whether the user set max_tokens or got a default (AgentConfig.max_tokens is only Some when set), so the exit-code decision can be made per case.
• **Size-gate hazard:** `src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs` is at 2036 lines, past the 2000 cap and not on the exemption list. 14 more lines and `cargo test` fails, which reverts the whole task.
• **No gap in hooks:** a pre-hook that can't start or times out already blocks the tool. Claude Code only just added that option.
• **yoagent 0.25.4 isn't worth upgrading to now:** its one change is to ToolGate, which yoyo doesn't use.

I also saved today's Claude Code 2.1.296–2.1.300 changelog comparison to yopedia.
